the knowledge base loop includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/loop.dmn".

the apply url of the eligible of the next steps is "https://tax-services.phila.gov/_/".

the help url of the eligible of the next steps is "https://www.phila.gov/services/payments-assistance-taxes/payment-plans-and-assistance-programs/income-based-programs-for-residents/apply-for-the-longtime-owner-occupants-program-loop/".

the help phone of the eligible of the next steps is "(215) 686-9200".

the body of the eligible of the next steps is "Use the Philadelphia Tax Center to find your property, open its OPA number, and choose the real estate assistance application. The program page also has a paper application.

- Include proof of income.
- Compare LOOP and Homestead savings before switching: you cannot receive both at once. Request Homestead removal with your LOOP application if needed.
- Applications are accepted throughout the year. Apply by September 30 for the benefit to apply to that year's bill.".

the note of the ineligible of the next steps is "Receiving the Homestead Exemption does not stop you from applying for LOOP, but you must request Homestead removal when applying. Use the City's property tax calculator to compare the programs first.".

rule checks_1 with provenance the model at decision checks:
the not already enrolled of the checks is true if
    the enrollments of the situation are listed
    and the primary person id of the situation is a text
    and it is not the case that
        the enrollments of the situation include a person id with a benefit
        and the primary person id of the situation is the text
        and the person id is equal to the text
        and the benefit is equal to "PhlLoop".

rule checks_2 with provenance the model at decision checks:
the not already enrolled of the checks is false if
    the enrollments of the situation are listed
    and the enrollments of the situation include a person id with a benefit
    and the person id is equal to the primary person id of the situation
    and the benefit is equal to "PhlLoop".

rule owner_occupant_service_1 with provenance the model at decision OwnerOccupantService:
the owner occupant service result is true if
    the owner occupant of the simple checks of the situation is true.

rule owner_occupant_service_2 with provenance the model at decision OwnerOccupantService:
the owner occupant service result is false if
    the owner occupant of the simple checks of the situation is false.

the owner occupant of the checks is the owner occupant service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

rule lives_in_philadelphia_pa_service_1 with provenance the model at decision LivesInPhiladelphiaPaService:
the lives in philadelphia pa service result is true if
    the lives in philadelphia pa of the simple checks of the situation is true.

rule lives_in_philadelphia_pa_service_2 with provenance the model at decision LivesInPhiladelphiaPaService:
the lives in philadelphia pa service result is false if
    the lives in philadelphia pa of the simple checks of the situation is false.

the lives in philadelphia pa of the checks is the lives in philadelphia pa service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

rule min_years_owner_occupant_service_1 with provenance the model at decision MinYearsOwnerOccupantService:
the min years owner occupant service result is true if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the years owner occupied of the situation is a number
        or the years owner occupied of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or 10 < 0
    and the years owner occupied of the situation is a number M
    and M >= 10.

rule min_years_owner_occupant_service_2 with provenance the model at decision MinYearsOwnerOccupantService:
the min years owner occupant service result is false if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the years owner occupied of the situation is a number
        or the years owner occupied of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or 10 < 0
    and the years owner occupied of the situation is a number M
    and M < 10.

the ten years owner occupant of the checks is the min years owner occupant service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

rule property_assessment_increase_service_1 with provenance the model at decision PropertyAssessmentIncreaseService:
the one year increase of the property assessment increase service is true if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the property assessment of the situation is a number
        or the property assessment of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or the previous year property assessment of the situation is a number M
                and M <= 0
                or it is not the case that the previous year property assessment of the situation is a third number
    and the property assessment of the situation is a number K
    and the previous year property assessment of the situation is a number P
    and K >= P * (1 + 50 / 100).

rule property_assessment_increase_service_2 with provenance the model at decision PropertyAssessmentIncreaseService:
the one year increase of the property assessment increase service is false if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the property assessment of the situation is a number
        or the property assessment of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or the previous year property assessment of the situation is a number M
                and M <= 0
                or it is not the case that the previous year property assessment of the situation is a third number
    and the property assessment of the situation is a number K
    and the previous year property assessment of the situation is a number P
    and K < P * (1 + 50 / 100).

rule property_assessment_increase_service_3 with provenance the model at decision PropertyAssessmentIncreaseService:
the five year increase of the property assessment increase service is true if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the property assessment of the situation is a number
        or the property assessment of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a number M
                and M <= 0
                or it is not the case that the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a third number
    and the property assessment of the situation is a number K
    and the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a number P
    and K >= P * (1 + 75 / 100).

rule property_assessment_increase_service_4 with provenance the model at decision PropertyAssessmentIncreaseService:
the five year increase of the property assessment increase service is false if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the property assessment of the situation is a number
        or the property assessment of the situation is a number N
            and N < 0
            or the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a number M
                and M <= 0
                or it is not the case that the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a third number
    and the property assessment of the situation is a number K
    and the lowest property assessment last five years of the situation is a number P
    and K < P * (1 + 75 / 100).

rule property_assessment_increase_service_5 with provenance the model at decision PropertyAssessmentIncreaseService:
the property assessment increase service result is true if
    the one year increase of the property assessment increase service is true.

rule property_assessment_increase_service_6 with provenance the model at decision PropertyAssessmentIncreaseService:
the property assessment increase service result is true if
    the five year increase of the property assessment increase service is true.

rule property_assessment_increase_service_7 with provenance the model at decision PropertyAssessmentIncreaseService:
the property assessment increase service result is false if
    the one year increase of the property assessment increase service is false
    and the five year increase of the property assessment increase service is false.

the assessment increase of the checks is the property assessment increase service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

rule tax_delinquent_service_1 with provenance the model at decision TaxDelinquentService:
the tax delinquent service result is true if
    the tax delinquent of the simple checks of the situation is true.

rule tax_delinquent_service_2 with provenance the model at decision TaxDelinquentService:
the tax delinquent service result is false if
    the tax delinquent of the simple checks of the situation is false.

rule property_taxes_current_or_payment_plan_service_1 with provenance the model at decision PropertyTaxesCurrentOrPaymentPlanService:
the property taxes current or payment plan service result is true if
    the tax delinquent service result is false.

rule property_taxes_current_or_payment_plan_service_2 with provenance the model at decision PropertyTaxesCurrentOrPaymentPlanService:
the property taxes current or payment plan service result is true if
    the property tax payment plan of the simple checks of the situation is true.

rule property_taxes_current_or_payment_plan_service_3 with provenance the model at decision PropertyTaxesCurrentOrPaymentPlanService:
the property taxes current or payment plan service result is false if
    the tax delinquent service result is true
    and the property tax payment plan of the simple checks of the situation is false.

the taxes current or payment plan of the checks is the property taxes current or payment plan service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

rule loop_income_service_1 with provenance the model at decision LoopIncomeService:
the loop income service result is true if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the household income of the situation is a number N
        or the household income of the situation is N
            and N < 0
            or it is not the case that the household size of the situation is a number M
    and it is not the case that
        the household size of the situation is M
        and M < 1
        or the household size of the situation is M
            and the count of the list [103050, 117800, 132500, 147200, 159000, 170800, 182550, 194350, 206100, 217900] is a number K
            and M > K
            or the household size of the situation is M
                and the household size of the situation is M
                and it is not the case that M = floor(M)
    and the household income of the situation is N
    and the household size of the situation is M
    and the item at position M of the list [103050, 117800, 132500, 147200, 159000, 170800, 182550, 194350, 206100, 217900] is a value V
    and N < V.

rule loop_income_service_2 with provenance the model at decision LoopIncomeService:
the loop income service result is false if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the household income of the situation is a number N
        or the household income of the situation is N
            and N < 0
            or it is not the case that the household size of the situation is a number M
    and it is not the case that
        the household size of the situation is M
        and M < 1
        or the household size of the situation is M
            and the count of the list [103050, 117800, 132500, 147200, 159000, 170800, 182550, 194350, 206100, 217900] is a number K
            and M > K
            or the household size of the situation is M
                and the household size of the situation is M
                and it is not the case that M = floor(M)
    and the household income of the situation is N
    and the household size of the situation is M
    and the item at position M of the list [103050, 117800, 132500, 147200, 159000, 170800, 182550, 194350, 206100, 217900] is a value V
    and N >= V.

the meets income requirement of the checks is the loop income service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

rule no_disqualifying_tax_abatement_service_1 with provenance the model at decision NoDisqualifyingTaxAbatementService:
the no disqualifying tax abatement service result is true if
    the disqualifying tax abatement of the simple checks of the situation is false.

rule no_disqualifying_tax_abatement_service_2 with provenance the model at decision NoDisqualifyingTaxAbatementService:
the no disqualifying tax abatement service result is false if
    the disqualifying tax abatement of the simple checks of the situation is true.

the no disqualifying tax abatement of the checks is the no disqualifying tax abatement service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

rule is_eligible_1 with provenance the model at decision isEligible:
the is_eligible is true if
    the not already enrolled of the checks is true
    and the owner occupant of the checks is true
    and the lives in philadelphia pa of the checks is true
    and the ten years owner occupant of the checks is true
    and the assessment increase of the checks is true
    and the taxes current or payment plan of the checks is true
    and the meets income requirement of the checks is true
    and the no disqualifying tax abatement of the checks is true.

